{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(items, pattern):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a sequence of items follows the given pattern sequence.\n    This involves establishing a bijective mapping between pattern tokens and item tokens.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize inputs to string lists to handle various hashable types.\n    normalized_items = [str(item) for item in items]\n    normalized_pattern = [str(p_token) for p_token in pattern]\n\n    # Sequences must have the same length to be considered a match.\n    if len(normalized_items) != len(normalized_pattern):\n        return False\n\n    # Dictionaries to store the bijective mapping: pattern_token -> item_token and vice versa.\n    pat2item = {}\n    item2pat = {}\n\n    # Iterate through both sequences simultaneously to build and check mappings.\n    for item, p_token in zip(normalized_items, normalized_pattern):\n        # Check consistency for the mapping from pattern token to item token.\n        if p_token in pat2item:\n            if pat2item[p_token] != item:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If the pattern token is new, ensure the item token is not already mapped to a different pattern token.\n            if item in item2pat:\n                if item2pat[item] != p_token:\n                    return False\n            \n            # Establish new mappings for unseen tokens.\n            pat2item[p_token] = item\n            item2pat[item] = p_token\n            \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "def find_tuples(tuples, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples from a list where all elements are divisible by k.\n    Assumes all input elements are integers and k is a non-zero integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    matching_tuples = []\n    for tup in tuples:\n        all_divisible = True\n        for element in tup:\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_divisible = False\n                break\n        if all_divisible:\n            matching_tuples.append(tup)\n    return matching_tuples"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff (number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum rule.\n    The rule sums digits at odd positions and subtracts digits at even positions;\n    if the result is divisible by 11, the original number is.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(number).lstrip('-')\n    total = 0\n    sign = 1\n    for ch in reversed(s):\n        total = (total + sign * (ord(ch) - 48)) % 11\n        sign = -sign\n    return total % 11 == 0"}
