{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(items: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    Assumes the input list is non-empty and contains hashable items.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    # Count the frequency of each item.\n    counts = Counter(items)\n\n    # Return the item that appears most frequently.\n    # most_common(1) returns a list containing one (item, count) tuple.\n    return counts.most_common(1)[0][0]"}
