{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Sequence, Any\n\ndef zero_count(seq: Sequence[Any]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in a sequence of numbers.\n    Assumes all sequence elements are convertible to int.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Count zeroes and non-zeroes. Per constraints, no explicit input validation or\n    # exception raising for non-convertible items is performed in this function.\n    zeros = sum(1 for x in seq if int(x) == 0)\n    nonzeros = sum(1 for x in seq if int(x) != 0)\n\n    # Compute ratio based on defined business rules.\n    if nonzeros > 0:\n        return zeros / nonzeros\n    elif zeros > 0: # nonzeros is 0, but there are zeros\n        return math.inf\n    else: # Both zeros and nonzeros are 0 (empty sequence)\n        return 0.0"}
