{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even (1-indexed) bits of the given number up to its most significant bit.\"\"\"\n    # Determine the effective bit width of the number, ensuring a minimum of 1.\n    width = max(1, n.bit_length())\n\n    # The pattern 0b10 sets the 0-indexed bit 1 (which corresponds to 1-indexed bit 2).\n    # This pattern will be shifted and combined to cover all 1-indexed even positions.\n    pattern = 0b10\n    \n    repeated_mask_builder = 0\n    current_shift = 0\n    \n    # Build a mask by repeatedly shifting and OR-ing the pattern.\n    while current_shift < width:\n        repeated_mask_builder |= (pattern << current_shift)\n        current_shift += 2 # Move to the next 1-indexed even bit position\n    \n    # Truncate the repeated pattern to the required width.\n    # This ensures only bits within the determined width are set.\n    mask = repeated_mask_builder & ((1 << width) - 1)\n    \n    # Apply the generated mask to the number using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return n | mask"}
