{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(list_of_tuples):\n    # Initialize a dictionary to store the counts of normalized tuples.\n    counts = {}\n\n    for item in list_of_tuples:\n        # Normalize the tuple by sorting its elements to ensure (a, b) and (b, a) are treated identically.\n        normalized_tuple = tuple(sorted(item))\n\n        # Increment the count for the normalized tuple in the dictionary.\n        counts[normalized_tuple] = counts.get(normalized_tuple, 0) + 1\n\n    return counts"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of sequences of length n meeting the criteria. Each element must be a positive integer, greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and less than or equal to m.\"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_from(min_val: int, remaining: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Recursively counts sequences starting with a value >= min_val for 'remaining' elements. Results are memoized to optimize performance.\"\"\"\n        if (min_val, remaining) in memo:\n            return memo[(min_val, remaining)]\n\n        if min_val > m:\n            # If the minimum required value is already greater than m, no sequence is possible.\n            return 0\n            \n        if remaining == 1:\n            # For the last element, any value from min_val to m is valid.\n            result = m - min_val + 1\n            memo[(min_val, remaining)] = result\n            return result\n\n        total_sequences = 0\n        # Calculate the maximum possible value for the current element (x)\n        # to ensure the remaining (remaining-1) elements can fit within m.\n        # The last element will be at least x * (2**(remaining-1)).\n        # Since the last element must be <= m, x * (2**(remaining-1)) <= m.\n        # This implies x <= m // (2**(remaining-1)).\n        max_possible_x = m // (2**(remaining - 1))\n\n        # Iterate through possible values for the current element 'x'.\n        # 'x' must be at least 'min_val' and at most 'm'.\n        # Additionally, 'x' must not exceed 'max_possible_x' to ensure the sequence can be completed.\n        for x in range(min_val, min(m, max_possible_x) + 1):\n            # Recursively count sequences for the rest of the elements.\n            # The next element must be at least 2*x.\n            total_sequences += _count_from(2 * x, remaining - 1)\n\n        memo[(min_val, remaining)] = total_sequences\n        return total_sequences\n\n    # The first element of the sequence must be a positive integer, so its minimum allowed value is 1.\n    return _count_from(1, n)"}
