{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\ndef dog_age(human_years: int) -> int:\n    # Calculate a dog's age in dog years using the specified conversion rules.\n    # The first two human years count as 10.5 dog years each.\n    # Each subsequent human year counts as 4 dog years.\n    FIRST_TWO_YEARS_RATE = 10.5\n    SUBSEQUENT_YEARLY_RATE = 4.0\n\n    if human_years <= 0:\n        dog_years_float = 0.0\n    elif human_years == 1:\n        dog_years_float = FIRST_TWO_YEARS_RATE\n    elif human_years == 2:\n        dog_years_float = FIRST_TWO_YEARS_RATE * 2\n    else:\n        dog_years_float = FIRST_TWO_YEARS_RATE * 2 + (human_years - 2) * SUBSEQUENT_YEARLY_RATE\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer using the round-half-up policy.\n    return int(Decimal(dog_years_float).quantize(Decimal('0'), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements of two tuple sequences element-wise.\n    It returns a new tuple of tuples where each element is the maximum of the corresponding input elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _elementwise_max(t1, t2):\n        \"\"\"Computes the element-wise maximum for two sequences.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(max(x, y) for x, y in zip(t1, t2))\n\n    a_tuples = tuple(tuple(inner) for inner in a)\n    b_tuples = tuple(tuple(inner) for inner in b)\n\n    result = tuple(_elementwise_max(t1, t2) for t1, t2 in zip(a_tuples, b_tuples))\n    return result"}
