{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "from fractions import Fraction\n\ndef parabola_directrix(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the directrix of a parabola y = a x^2 + b x + c.\n    Returns a Fraction if all inputs are integers, otherwise returns a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine if exact fraction arithmetic should be used based on input types.\n    if isinstance(a, int) and isinstance(b, int) and isinstance(c, int):\n        a_val = Fraction(a)\n        b_val = Fraction(b)\n        c_val = Fraction(c)\n        \n        # Directrix formula: y = c - (b^2 + 1) / (4a)\n        return c_val - (b_val * b_val + Fraction(1)) / (Fraction(4) * a_val)\n    else:\n        # Use float arithmetic if any input is not an integer.\n        a_val = float(a)\n        b_val = float(b)\n        c_val = float(c)\n        \n        # Directrix formula: y = c - (b^2 + 1) / (4a)\n        return c_val - (b_val * b_val + 1.0) / (4.0 * a_val)"}
